      "message": "\u003e Existing implementation in host driver sets the Root Table pointer early during initialization followed by context/pasid updates for all devices and then towards the end of the iommu initialization we enable translation. context/pasid updates invoke a cache flush which calls into qi_submit_sync(). These flushes were not needed as translation was not enabled, but since the code for context/pasid updates needed to handle cases with or without translation enabled, so it did call the flush.\n\nI see, thx.\n\nStill I\u0027m just curious where exactly in the code we do context/pasid updates for all devices after iommu_set_root_entry() but before iommu_enable_translation(). I haven\u0027t quickly found that in the code. Could you point at where that is done?",
